<title>ITALY: Fiat denies talks with Automakers.</title>
<headline>Fiat denies talks with Automakers.</headline>
<dateline>TURIN, Italy 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokesman for Italian carmaker Fiat Auto SpA denied rumours it was in talks to take a stake in South Africa's Automakers Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;The talk is completely unfounded&quot;, he told Reuters.</p>
<p>Shares in Johannesburg-based Automakers soared on Friday amid talk the firm was in talks with Japan's Nissan and Fiat on a possible tie-up.</p>
<p>Automakers, the holding company of Nissan South Africa Ltd, builds and sells Fiat and Nissan models under licence.</p>
<p>Dealers and analysts in South Africa have speculated one or both of the firms are in talks with Automakers' main shareholder Sankorp over the sale of its 50.7 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
